    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1393">

                <pb facs="1097" n="981" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg981"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 412.11 H141/5.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1793.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 30, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to this Embassy’s despatch of
                    August 30th last. No. 1625,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1393-f1"/> regarding the claim
                    of Mr. Herbert L. Hall, I have the honor to transmit herewith a copy in
                    translation of a recent note from the Minister for Foreign Affairs in reply to
                    the Embassy’s representations in this matter.</p>
                <pb facs="1098" n="982" xml:id="pg982"/>
                <p>It will be observed that in this note the Mexican Government takes a positive
                    attitude towards such claims for losses suffered by foreigners by revolutions
                    and one which, if concurred in by the Department, will render useless any
                    further steps towards the collection of damages for losses suffered by American
                    interests in Mexico arising from the revolutionary movements of the past two
                    years.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Montgomery Schuyler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1393-a1.xml" xpointer="d1393-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
